  You are an independent, adversarial reviewer. Another engineer implemented this task in the worktree /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/wf_cd627354-1a0-2. The unmodified base tree is /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/wave2-base. Do NOT edit anything in either tree and do NOT run git (it is refused). Compare the two with `diff -ru` on the relevant crate src and tests directories (exclude target/), and read the changed files in full.

  TASK THEY WERE GIVEN:
  You are working on the Callisto repository (Rust workspace: callisto-model MIT, callisto-manifests, callisto-graph, callisto-cli). You were started in your own git worktree, created from the base tree /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/wave2-base (current main plus the open #223 change that adds DepLocator). Work only inside your worktree; never edit /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/wave2-base or any other path.

  HARD CONSTRAINTS
  - git commands are refused in this sandbox. Do NOT commit, branch, push or open PRs: leave your change uncommitted. Use ordinary file tools and cargo.
  - Do NOT run `just ci`, `just coverage` or a whole-workspace test: the coordinator runs the full gate serially. Run only scoped checks for the crate(s) you touch: `cargo test -p <crate> ...`, `cargo clippy -p <crate> --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo fmt -p <crate>`. One cargo command at a time.
  - Repository rules (AGENTS.md): safe Rust only; TOML edits go through toml_edit and JSON edits preserve key order and indentation, never regex or line edits; file writes go through callisto_model::atomic::atomic_write; user-facing errors derive miette::Diagnostic with a code and a help line; no emojis; code comments are one short line and only for a non-obvious why, never history ("previously", "used to", "no longer"); never cite spec IDs, criterion IDs or section numbers in code, comments, test names or messages; no cargo features.
