   "stopped_early": false,
   "summary": "Python requirements are now addressed per declaration like Cargo. Each declaration in `[project].dependencies`, in each extra, and in `[tool.poetry.dependencies]` gets its own edge and its own `DepLocator`, so each is rewritten from its own constraint.\n\nSETUP NOTE. My worktree did not contain the #223 change, because it is uncommitted in the base tree. I copied `crates/` and `.changeset/noble-foxes-climb.md` from `wave2-base` into this worktree, read-only on the base side. The coordinator should diff against base to isolate my change. My edits are in the files listed under files_changed.\n\nREPRODUCTION. I ran the new black-box tests against the unfixed writer with the real binary.\n- Scenario A (extras `a=[\"lib-py>=0.1\"]`, `c=[\"lib-py==0.1.0\"]`): the result was `a = [\"lib-py==0.2.0\"]` and `c = [\"lib-py==0.1.0\"]`. The loose extra was rewritten with the pin's constraint and the stale pin stayed.\n- Scenario B (two marker lines in `dependencies`): only the first line was rewritten, giving `lib-py==0.2.0;python_version<'3.9'` while the second stayed `==0.1.0`.\n- A `>=0.1` line before a `==0.1.0` line in `dependencies` had the loose line rewritten and the pin left stale.\n- `Lib_Py[x]==0.1.0` plus `lib.py==0.1.0`: only the first was rewritten.\n\nDESIGN.\n- `DepLocator` in callisto-model gains `container: Option<DepContainer>` and `position: Option<usize>`. It is now `#[non_exhaustive]`.\n- New enum `DepContainer` has three variants: `ProjectDependencies`, `Extra(String)` and `PoetryDependencies`.\n- Constructors are `DepLocator::cargo(section, target)` and `DepLocator::python(container, position)`.\n- `iter_dependencies` enumerates each requirement array before filtering, so `position` is the raw array index even when the graph skips unparseable or non-string entries. Poetry edges carry `PoetryDependencies` with no position, because that table is keyed by name.\n- `update_dependency_spec` for Python is now strict and addresses exactly one declaration. A missing, default or inapplicable locator returns `DependencyNotFound`.\n- It checks at write time that the requirement at the position still has the same normalized name, and otherwise returns `DependencyNotFound` and writes nothing. That check reuses the existing `rewrite_requirement` name guard.\n- The first-match-and-break logic and the \"1b. Extras\" reference-constraint logic are removed.\n- Cargo and npm behaviour is unchanged. The Cargo call site and the two graph test call sites were migrated to `DepLocator::cargo`.\n\nBEHAVIOUR NOTE. Because the dependent releases, the existing floor-raise pass rewrites every declaration of a co-released dependency, as it does for plain requirements. In scenario A the loose `a = [\"lib-py>=0.1\"]` therefore becomes `>=0.2.0` from its own constraint. The existing test `an_extra_with_a_different_constraint_is_left_as_written` asserted the old defect, since `wide = [\"lib-py>=0.1,<0.3\"]` was left alone. I renamed it to `an_extra_range_that_still_covers_the_new_version_has_its_floor_raised_like_a_plain_requirement` and it now expects `>=0.2.0, <1`, the same result a plain `[project.dependencies]` entry gets from `round_trip`.\n\nSIBLING DEFECT FIXED IN THE SAME CHANGE. The Poetry writer replaced a whole dotted-table or inline-table dependency with a bare string for dotted tables, which dropped `extras` and other keys. It now sets only `version` on any table-like item. A unit test covers this. I did not confirm that test fails on the old code.\n\nNOT DONE.\n- Poetry groups (`[tool.poetry.group.*]`) and `[dependency-groups]` are not read by the code, so I added no support, as instructed.\n- A rewritten requirement line still loses the space after `;`. For example `b==1;python_version<'3.9'` comes out without the space because `Requirement::render` omits it. That is existing behaviour, unchanged. Markers are preserved but the line is normalized.\n- Poetry bare versions such as `\"0.1.0\"` and caret ranges such as `^0.1.0` are Opaque or not round-trippable. That is existing behaviour. My Poetry test uses `==0.1.0`.\n\nCHANGESET. I did not edit `.changeset`.\n- Sentence to delete from `.changeset/noble-foxes-climb.md`: \"A Python requirement declared twice with different constraints, in two extras or with two markers, is still followed by its first declaration only.\"\n- Suggested replacement heading: \"**A dependency declared more than once is followed and rewritten in each declaration**\".\n- Suggested body: \"A dependency declared more than once, for example in `[dependencies]` and a `[target.<cfg>.dependencies]` table in Cargo, or in `[project].dependencies` and an extra, or under two markers in a Python manifest, now cascades to its dependent and is rewritten in every declaration when the package it names is released, each from its own constraint. Before, only the first declaration was updated, or another declaration was overwritten with the first one's constraint. A declaration whose range still covers the new version has its lower bound raised, as a plain declaration does.\"\n- Suggested Breaking additions: \"`callisto_model`: `DepLocator` is `#[non_exhaustive]` and gains `container: Option<DepContainer>` and `position: Option<usize>`; build one with `DepLocator::cargo` or `DepLocator::python`. `DepContainer` is new. Python declarations now carry a locator, so `DepLocator::default()` is the value for npm only. `callisto_manifests`: the Python `update_dependency_spec` returns `DependencyNotFound` for a locator that does not address a declaration.\" Also change the existing line \"`DepLocator::default()` is the value for npm and Python declarations\" to say npm only.",
